WEBVTT

00:10:59.208 --> 00:11:02.101
AG: Steamrolling was
in Jason Botterill's blood.

00:11:02.125 --> 00:11:04.601
For a while, he was a pro hockey player.

00:11:04.625 --> 00:11:06.434
He was a bruiser.

00:11:06.458 --> 00:11:09.601
After one too many concussions,
his career was cut short,

00:11:09.625 --> 00:11:12.351
and he decided to get
into hockey management.

00:11:12.375 --> 00:11:15.101
When Jason enrolled
in my negotiation class,

00:11:15.125 --> 00:11:18.226
I quickly saw that he was
just as tough off the ice.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:21.434
JB: Well, I think it was
similar to my playing days.

00:11:21.458 --> 00:11:25.184
You'll do a little bit of a hook
or a penalty on the ice

00:11:25.208 --> 00:11:28.059
and the ref doesn't see it,
no issues with it and stuff.

00:11:28.083 --> 00:11:29.351
You're just trying to win.

00:11:29.375 --> 00:11:31.226
I brought some of that competitiveness